&lt;p&gt;Maven Securities is a leading proprietary trading firm that uses sophisticated technology and quantitative analysis to trade global financial markets. We specialise in options and derivatives market making, where your skills can have a real impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Maven, we believe exceptional careers are built deliberately. Our summer internship is designed for a small number of high-potential students each year, combining structured training with practical exposure. We don’t hire large classes expecting only a few to succeed; we invest in every individual who joins the programme.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programme details&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; London&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programme dates:&lt;/strong&gt; 21st June – 20th August 2027&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application deadline:&lt;/strong&gt; 21st October 2026&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key requirements: &lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You must have the right to work in the region you are applying for at the time of application&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You must be a penultimate-year undergraduate or master’s student&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You must not have applied for any other Maven programmes in this cycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join a structured nine-week internship in our London office, giving you a practical introduction to options market making. The programme starts with options theory before quickly progressing to trading simulation and mock trading, helping you build the foundations you need to become a trader. You’ll also gain exposure to different desks through shadowing and project work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Throughout the internship, you’ll be assessed on your performance and development. Successful interns may be considered for our Graduate Trader Programme the following year.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build practical trading skills in our simulation environment, applying your learning to real market scenarios&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use the same tools as our traders - or build your own - and observe the same trades being executed in the live market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn directly from traders across different desks through shadowing and regular interaction, with opportunities to ask questions and understand their day-to-day approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take part in a dedicated Reading Week, working independently on a project and exploring an area of interest&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How and what you will learn&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build your foundations in options market making - we don’t expect prior knowledge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop your understanding of options theory, pricing, probability and risk with Maven’s in-house trainers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply your knowledge through trading simulation, testing different strategies, learning from experience and building confidence as a trader&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop your understanding of the wider market through macroeconomics and technical training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Progress through clear learning milestones, with ongoing feedback from the Trading and Emerging Talent teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key criteria&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong numeracy skills and a good understanding of probability and statistics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine interest in financial markets and a curiosity to learn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A willingness to adopt and utilise emerging AI technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re looking for someone who is&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An entrepreneurial thinker&lt;/strong&gt; who takes the initiative to generate ideas that further your learning and improve existing tools or systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A critical problem solver and decision-maker&lt;/strong&gt; who analyses situations and makes effective decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An agile learner&lt;/strong&gt; who quickly acquires knowledge, responds to feedback and adapts to new situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Able to synthesise information&lt;/strong&gt; and turn complex or conflicting inputs into clear, actionable insights and decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative and influential&lt;/strong&gt;, able to build trust, share what you have learned and work effectively with others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Results-focused and accountable&lt;/strong&gt;, comfortable taking ownership and making decisions in the face of uncertainty and with incomplete information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Maven?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dedicated in-house trainers:&lt;/strong&gt; Learn through a programme designed for the Summer Trader Internship and delivered by Maven’s traders and in-house experts, covering technical and professional skills, as well as how AI is integrated into our daily work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accelerate your career:&lt;/strong&gt; Learn by trying new things, making mistakes and developing quickly. We’ve had traders progress to head-of-desk roles within two and a half years of joining as graduates. If you perform well and are ready, you can progress quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven pathways:&lt;/strong&gt; Around a quarter of our workforce joined through an Emerging Talent Programme, including more than 50 of our current traders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Supported to succeed:&lt;/strong&gt; Receive regular feedback, structured reviews and day-to-day support, including a Maven buddy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We invest in you:&lt;/strong&gt; From the start of the internship, you’ll be immersed in a simulated trading environment and learn directly from traders. Throughout, you’ll gain practical insight into how our desks operate and have the opportunity to demonstrate your potential for the Graduate Trader Programme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Maven is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to building a diverse workforce and inclusive environment. We welcome applications from all candidates regardless of background or identity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits at Maven&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an intern, you’ll be eligible for benefits including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular social events where you can get to know us, from welcome dinners and the Maven summer party to end-of-programme celebrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free daily breakfast and lunch in the office, as well as snacks and drinks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;On-site gym access, with regular classes and in-office massages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A forward-thinking environment in which AI is integral to our strategy and daily operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Software Developer Summer Internship London 2027&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Maven Securities is a leading proprietary trading firm that leverages sophisticated technology and quantitative analysis to trade in global financial markets. We specialise in options and derivatives market making, where your skills can be directly applied to have a real impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Maven, we believe exceptional careers are built deliberately. Our intern programme is designed for a small number of high-potential individuals each year, combining comprehensive training, real responsibility, and long-term development. We don’t hire large classes with the expectation that only a few will succeed, we invest in every individual who joins the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programme details:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; London&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programme dates:&lt;/strong&gt; 21st June - 20 August 2027&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application deadline:&lt;/strong&gt; 21st October 2026&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key requirements: &lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You must have the right to work in the region you are applying for at the time of application&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You must be a penultimate-year undergraduate or master’s student&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You must not have applied for any other Maven programmes in this cycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll begin with a structured 2-week training programme, designed to prepare you for your project work. This initial phase focuses on building the technical foundations and domain knowledge needed for the projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Following training, you’ll transition on to a 7-week project, where you’ll continue to learn through hands-on experience. Intern projects allow you to learn new skills and experience what life is like in a Maven Technology team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be directly embedded in Maven engineering teams to work on real world problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a direct impact on the day-to-day workings of a high performance trading firm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate directly with Developers and Traders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How and what you will learn:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Progress through a structured onboarding programme with clear learning milestones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build your foundation through theory and exercise-led training, led by Maven’s Head of Technology Training &amp;amp; Graduates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain in-depth insight to the work you could expect to be doing as a future Graduate Developer by attending desk shadowing opportunities with current Graduates, across a range of Technology teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our technical syllabus covers the fundamentals of some of Maven’s main programming languages, e.g. C++, C# and Python, as well as TypeScript and ReactWe will teach you how to use some of Maven’s in-house tools and systems. Maven utilises the latest technology in order to meet and exceed our demanding business challenges. We believe in using the right tool for the right job with a strong focus on engineering rigour&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend regular check-ins with the Technology and Emerging Talent teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key criteria:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine interest in software development and a curiosity to learn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with one or more programming languages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A willingness to adopt and utilise emerging AI technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re looking for someone who is:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An entrepreneurial thinker&lt;/strong&gt; with the ability to generate ideas, take initiative and drive innovation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A critical problem solver and decision maker&lt;/strong&gt; who can analyse situations, think clearly and make effective decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An agile learner&lt;/strong&gt; who is able to quickly acquire knowledge, take on feedback, adapt and apply insights across different contexts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Able to synthesise information&lt;/strong&gt;, resolve conflicting inputs, see the bigger picture, and translate complex information into actionable recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative and influential&lt;/strong&gt;, able to build trust, work effectively with others and positively impact the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Results-focused and accountable&lt;/strong&gt;, taking ownership and delivering outcomes reliably&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Maven?:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dedicated In-House Trainers:&lt;/strong&gt; Gain the tools to succeed in a rapidly evolving market, where AI is integral to our strategy and daily operations. Our tailored curriculums are led by in-house experts and cover both technical and professional skills, as well as guidance on how to adopt AI best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accelerate Your Career:&lt;/strong&gt; Over 9 weeks, you’ll progress your understanding of software development and have the opportunity to jump-start your Maven career by being considered for a full-time Graduate Developer role for the following year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven Pathways:&lt;/strong&gt; Benefit from our structured pipeline programmes that set you up for long-term success. Around a quarter of Maven’s workforce joined through an Emerging Talent Programme, with many staying from Spring Week through the Graduate Programme and beyond&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Supported to Succeed&lt;/strong&gt;:&amp;nbsp;We are committed to fostering an inclusive workplace where everyone can perform at your best. We offer recruitment support where needed, and employee resource groups that help build community across the firm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grow with Guidance:&lt;/strong&gt; Enjoy regular feedback, structured review points, and informal off-desk chats. Everyone in our Emerging Talent Programmes is also paired with a Maven buddy for practical advice and day-to-day support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make a Real Impact, Fast:&lt;/strong&gt; Interns are embedded directly into our tech teams, contributing to critical projects. In fact, recent interns contributed to the foundations of Maven&#39;s AI initiative, which includes creating agentic workflows for different business functions, improving Trader and Developer tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Maven is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to building a diverse workforce and creating an inclusive environment. We welcome applications from all candidates regardless of background or identity.&lt;/p&gt;
