&lt;p&gt;As an intern on our Central Execution Desk you will be working on cutting edge execution research, modeling, and execution performance evaluation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exploring execution and trading ideas by analysing market microstructure for patterns in liquidity, trading costs, and execution outcomes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building tools, simulations, and analytics to support trading and execution decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing to research libraries and production workflows for execution analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing and evaluating models; performing causal analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with large, noisy datasets and building robust data-processing and model-calibration pipelines&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A current student from a top-tier university pursuing a PhD in Mathematics, Statistics, Computer Science, Financial Engineering, Physics, Operations Research, Economics, or an equivalent quantitative discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong grounding in mathematics, statistics, optimization, and machine learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In depth data-mining and analysis skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming skills in one or more of Python, C++ and Rust&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An interest in in market microstructure, optimal execution, causal inference, and quantitative trading&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with large financial, tick, or order-book datasets, market microstructure, transaction cost analysis, market impact, simulation, or optimal execution is a plus but not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Internship can start on a timeline convenient to you, preferably within 6 months preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
