&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In your penultimate year of studying Economics, Econometrics, Finance or STEM, graduating in 2028&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated interest in the financial markets and macro economics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You want to make an impact on meaningful and challenging projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive working in an environment where creativity, teamwork, and innovation are recognised and rewarded&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding analytical and problem-solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a programming language is a plus (e.g. Python, Matlab, or R)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to start the internship on June 28, 2027&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
