&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;passionate and hands-on Event Producer Intern, who will support our Lead Producer in all aspects of production ensuring that high-quality experiences are delivered.&lt;/strong&gt; This person will be involved in all parts of event production for our DACH Market.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is an opportunity to learn and develop your production skills across different types of live events and experiences&lt;/strong&gt;. You will gain exposure to event planning, technical production, supplier coordination, budgeting, onsite execution, and post-event wrap-up, while supporting the wider team in bringing creative concepts to life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role &lt;strong&gt;requires flexibility, creativity, strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and a willingness to learn. &lt;/strong&gt;You should be comfortable working in a fast-paced environment, managing multiple tasks, and supporting the team to meet deadlines and deliver great experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate has some experience in live events, theatre, stage management, or another fast-paced operational environment, and is passionate about creating memorable experiences for audiences.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage all aspects of event productions, including pre-production logistics planning, vendor selection, hiring, onsite execution, as well as post-event wrap-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the wider Fever Originals team in the development of new events, implementing new production formats and ensuring Fever remains up to date, and ahead of the curve, on emerging technologies and solutions that can enhance Fever’s experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create productions timelines and ensure that teams are keeping to schedule&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess and manage budgets of different scales, working with project managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate and collaborate with internal cross-functional teams and stakeholders to drive alignment and execution of event deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage multiple productions and help scale various Fever Original event formats across the market&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle administrative duties including expense reports, invoicing, and working with the legal department on contracts&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domestic and international travel and work across time zones may be required&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You thrive in a fast-paced environment and pride yourself on your flexible, organized, and detail-oriented mindset. You have excellent communication skills. You have operational experience, but also an ability to think strategically from a business perspective.&lt;/p&gt;
